## andrej-karpathy-skills

https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills, cloned at `2c60614`.

**Unresolved, and the one to settle before publishing.** The repository states
"MIT" in its README and ships no `LICENSE` file, and the GitHub API reports no
licence for it. It is also not Andrej Karpathy's own repository: it is a third
party's compilation of his published guidelines, which our own `ATTRIBUTIONS.md`
misnamed until 2026-08-18. So there is no notice to preserve and no holder to
name with confidence, while `core/PRINCIPLES.md` P2 and P3 are close to that
text.

Two ways out, and both are work rather than paperwork: rewrite P2 and P3 from
our own practice the way the four claude.ai rules were rewritten, or ask the
repository owner for a licence file naming a holder. Until one of them is done,
this is the open item that blocks publication, not a formality.

## loopx

Apache-2.0, https://github.com/loopx-ai/loopx. Concept only: an eight-word
shingle comparison between their `self-repair` document and our `debug` plus
`GUARDRAILS` finds no overlap, so no expression of theirs is reproduced and no
derivative work is distributed. The full licence is not embedded for that
reason. If any wording of theirs ever lands here, this section becomes the
whole Apache-2.0 text plus their NOTICE.

## Published system prompts of claude.ai

Reading them prompted four rules (PS-017). They were rewritten from our own
practice on 2026-08-18, each resting on evidence from this repository and
folded into our own numbering — P6, G6 and the formatting section of
`core/OUTPUT.md`. No text of theirs ships, and none of their wording remains.
The acknowledgement stays because the questions were theirs.
